<section id="about" class="py-20 animate-slide-up">
  <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-8">
    About
  </h3>
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-12">
    <!-- Main Text Column -->
    <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        I'm a full-stack engineer with over six years of experience building
        distributed systems, financial platforms, and the products on top of
        them. I've led a team of four, owned architecture across client
        platforms, and been the only engineer responsible for a live product.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about the parts that break in production: idempotency and
        consistency when money moves, pipelines that survive flaky upstream
        sources, and integrations with partner APIs that were never designed to
        be easy. The through-line is data that has to stay correct while
        arriving from somewhere I don't control.
      </p>
      <p>
        More recently that work has moved into applied AI: agent orchestration
        on Google ADK, LLM-powered generation inside a shipped product, and
        computer vision systems from earlier in my career. The engineering
        problem there is rarely the model. It's the deterministic scaffolding
        that makes a probabilistic system's output something you can depend on.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Technical Focus Side Column -->
